**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/node_modules/
# Generated by svelte-kit sync, and the UI build output - both are produced inside the image, and
# copying a stale host build in would silently ship whatever was last built locally.
**/.svelte-kit/
CallTree.UI/build/
# Same reason, and it bites harder: if a locally staged wwwroot reaches the build stage, dotnet
# publish precompresses it to .br/.gz, and those survive the later COPY of the real UI (COPY
# overwrites files but never removes them). The container would then serve a stale compressed copy
# to any client sending Accept-Encoding.
CallTree.Core/CallTree.Api/wwwroot/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
deploy/
tools/
**/*.user
**/data/
**/coverage/
*.md
